      "hints": [
        "General term: $\\binom{6}{r}\\left(\\frac{2}{x}\\right)^{6-r}(-3x)^r = \\binom{6}{r}2^{6-r}(-3)^r x^{2r-6}$.",
        "Set $2r - 6 = 0 \\implies r = 3$.",
        "Evaluate $\\binom{6}{3}2^3(-3)^3 = -4320$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Write the general term $T_{r+1}$ in the binomial expansion of $\\left(\\frac{2}{x} - 3x\\right)^6$:\n$$T_{r+1} = \\binom{6}{r}\\left(\\frac{2}{x}\\right)^{6-r}(-3x)^r = \\binom{6}{r}2^{6-r}(-3)^r x^{r - (6-r)} = \\binom{6}{r}2^{6-r}(-3)^r x^{2r-6}$$",
        "To find the term independent of $x$, set the power of $x$ to $0$:\n$$2r - 6 = 0 \\implies 2r = 6 \\implies r = 3$$",
        "Evaluate the constant term for $r = 3$:\n$$\\text{Constant term} = \\binom{6}{3}2^{6-3}(-3)^3 = 20 \\times 8 \\times (-27) = -4320$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
